# Skill: save

Cursor adapter for the `save` skill. Full procedure (single source of truth):
`.claude/skills/save/SKILL.md` in this repo.

## When To Use

A quick mid-session checkpoint so the next session resumes the paper work. Lighter than `/handoff`.

## When Not To Use

A thorough end-of-session freeze (use `/handoff`); recording state by editing the manuscript.

## Workflow

Inspect state read-only: `git status --short` (parent), `git -C paper/overleaf status -s`. If a
durable, non-obvious fact emerged that git doesn't already record, write/update one memory file under
`~/.claude/projects/-home-dmbrmv-Development-camels-ru/memory/` (frontmatter `name`, `description`,
`metadata.type` ∈ user|feedback|project|reference) and refresh the `MEMORY.md` index line. If nothing
durable emerged, skip the memory write.

## Output Handling

Report whether auto-memory was updated (and which file), a one-line git-state summary, and the
shortest resume next-action.

## Safety Constraints

Never auto-commit or push. No secrets, transcripts, or credentials in memory. Do not invent a
`docs/sessions/` tree; a human-readable note (optional) appends to an existing doc only.
